{"type":"assistant","uuid":"8cca051a-51e3-4bfa-a7a9-ddf889d54802","session_id":"faf8342e-7876-4dfe-986a-5adecc31d677","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"8cca051a-51e3-4bfa-a7a9-ddf889d54802","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe fix is complete. Here's a summary of the patch:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/io/lerk/lrkFM/adapter/FileArrayAdapter.java`\n\n**Root Cause:** A `ConcurrentModificationException` was thrown because the code modified an `ArrayList` while iterating over it with a for-each loop. This happened in two places:\n\n1. **`removeFromContext()` (line 188 in original):** The for-each loop creates an `Iterator`, but calling `collection.remove()` inside the loop modifies the collection directly, causing the iterator to detect the modification and throw `ConcurrentModificationException`.\n\n2. **`initUI()` (lines 162-170):** The for-each loop called `checkBox.setChecked()` on each context file, which triggered the `OnCheckedChangeListener` to modify the same collection being iterated.\n\n**Fixes Applied:**\n\n| Change | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| **`removeFromContext()`** | Replaced for-each loop with explicit `Iterator` and `iterator.remove()` — the only safe way to remove elements during iteration |\n| **`initUI()` checkbox loop** | Replaced for-each loop with index-based iteration and hoisted the context list into a local variable |\n| **`updatingCheckBoxState` guard** | Added a boolean flag to prevent `setChecked()` calls (which fire the listener) from triggering recursive modifications during view initialization |\n\nThe patch is at `/tmp/bug-1568.patch` and the project compiles successfully."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39380,"output_tokens":355,"cache_read_input_tokens":37728,"total_tokens":39735}}}
